      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the moral argument for taking action is compelling, relying on sanctions as a substitute for war often justifies a policy of appeasement that allows tyrants to continue their abuses with impunity. History has shown that \"imperfect\" sanctions frequently fail to stop atrocities, instead creating a false sense of security while the status quo of oppression remains intact. True accountability requires decisive, targeted pressure that doesn't sacrifice human lives for the sake of political theater, rather than accepting a flawed compromise that lets bad actors off the hook.",
